You are given an integer array nums and two integers, x and k. You can perform the following operation any number of times (including zero):

Increase or decrease any element of nums by 1.
Return the minimum number of operations needed to have at least k non-overlapping subarrays of size exactly x in nums, where all elements within each subarray are equal.

 

Example 1:

Input: nums = [5,-2,1,3,7,3,6,4,-1], x = 3, k = 2

Output: 8

Explanation:

Use 3 operations to add 3 to nums[1] and use 2 operations to subtract 2 from nums[3]. The resulting array is [5, 1, 1, 1, 7, 3, 6, 4, -1].
Use 1 operation to add 1 to nums[5] and use 2 operations to subtract 2 from nums[6]. The resulting array is [5, 1, 1, 1, 7, 4, 4, 4, -1].
Now, all elements within each subarray [1, 1, 1] (from indices 1 to 3) and [4, 4, 4] (from indices 5 to 7) are equal. Since 8 total operations were used, 8 is the output.
Example 2:

Input: nums = [9,-2,-2,-2,1,5], x = 2, k = 2

Output: 3

Explanation:

Use 3 operations to subtract 3 from nums[4]. The resulting array is [9, -2, -2, -2, -2, 5].
Now, all elements within each subarray [-2, -2] (from indices 1 to 2) and [-2, -2] (from indices 3 to 4) are equal. Since 3 operations were used, 3 is the output.
 

Constraints:

2 <= nums.length <= 10^5
-10^6 <= nums[i] <= 10^6
2 <= x <= nums.length
1 <= k <= 15
2 <= k * x <= nums.length

Code:

class Solution {
    TreeMap<Integer, Integer> left = new TreeMap<>();
    TreeMap<Integer, Integer> right = new TreeMap<>();
    int leftSize = 0, rightSize = 0;
    long leftSum = 0, rightSum = 0;
    void add(TreeMap<Integer, Integer> map, int val) {
        map.put(val, map.getOrDefault(val, 0) + 1);
    }
    void remove(TreeMap<Integer, Integer> map, int val) {
        int count = map.get(val);
        if (count == 1) {
            map.remove(val);
        } else {
            map.put(val, count - 1);
        }
    }

    void insert(int val) {
        if (left.isEmpty() || val <= left.lastKey()) {
            add(left, val);
            leftSize++;
            leftSum += val;
        } else {
            add(right, val);
            rightSize++;
            rightSum += val;
        }
        balance();
    }

    void erase(int val) {
        if (left.containsKey(val)) {
            remove(left, val);
            leftSize--;
            leftSum -= val;
        } else {
            remove(right, val);
            rightSize--;
            rightSum -= val;
        }
        balance();
    }

    void balance() {
        while (leftSize > rightSize + 1) {
            int val = left.lastKey();
            remove(left, val);
            leftSize--;
            leftSum -= val;
            add(right, val);
            rightSize++;
            rightSum += val;
        }

        while (leftSize < rightSize) {
            int val = right.firstKey();
            remove(right, val);
            rightSize--;
            rightSum -= val;
            add(left, val);
            leftSize++;
            leftSum += val;
        }
    }
    long getCost() {
        long median = left.lastKey();
        long leftCost = median * leftSize - leftSum;
        long rightCost = rightSum - median * rightSize;
        return leftCost + rightCost;
    }

    public long minOperations(int[] nums, int x, int k) {
        int n = nums.length;
        // Step 1: Calculate cost of every window of size x
        long[] cost = new long[n - x + 1];
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            insert(nums[i]);
            if (i >= x) {
                erase(nums[i - x]);
            }
            if (i >= x - 1) {
                cost[i - x + 1] = getCost();
            }
        }
        // Step 2: DP
        long INF = Long.MAX_VALUE / 2;
        long[] prev = new long[n + 1];
        long[] curr = new long[n + 1];
        Arrays.fill(prev, INF);
        // Selecting zero subarrays requires zero operations
        Arrays.fill(prev, 0);
        for (int j = 1; j <= k; j++) {
            Arrays.fill(curr, INF);
            for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
                // Choice 1: Skip current element
                curr[i] = curr[i - 1];
                // Choice 2: Select a window ending at i - 1
                if (i >= x && prev[i - x] != INF) {
                    curr[i] = Math.min(
                        curr[i],
                        prev[i - x] + cost[i - x]
                    );
                }
            }
            prev = curr;
            curr = new long[n + 1];
        }
        return prev[n];
    }
}



Note:

Time Complexity:

Let:
n = Length of nums
x = Window size
k = Number of non-overlapping subarrays to select

Step    Operation                                  Time Complexity
-----------------------------------------------------------------
1       Insert element into TreeMap                O(log x)
2       Remove element from TreeMap               O(log x)
3       Balance two TreeMaps                       O(log x)
4       Calculate window cost using median/sums   O(1)
5       Calculate costs for all windows            O(n * log x)
6       DP transitions                             O(n * k)
-----------------------------------------------------------------

Overall Time Complexity:
O(n * log x + n * k)

= O(n * (log x + k))
